{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"tool_94SiFvQKhbLiZQ5sRqfCe6Y8","content":"1\tCreated-Local: 2026-11-02 01:5x +0700\n2\tCoding-Agent: kimi\n3\tSession: fresh (read-only architect ruling)\n4\tMode: read-only\n5\t\n6\t# Ruling needed: the PHPT stress cost — guest execution budget or re-tiering?\n7\t\n8\tFollow-up to the P4 heap work. The engineer's fixture-by-fixture walk (collab/1793540000000-engineer-p4-hang.gpt-6-luna.findings.md in worktree /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-php-p4) found NO unbounded guest fixture. The recorded shiva \"hangs\" in yang.php.antlr.e2e-test (93 min at 100% CPU; thread dump collab/orch-lane/p4-e2e-hang-threaddump.txt in the main checkout, stack: run_loop <- vm_step <- test-utils/run-vm) and the PHPT selection (33+ min) are now best explained as finite stress cases that are simply expensive: Zend/tests/gc_013.phpt runs a fixed 10,001-iteration loop and takes ~259 s on one VM, and e2e-test carries phpt-derived stress cases; under two concurrent lanes on shiva the wall clock multiplies.\n9\t\n10\t## The question\n11\t\n12\tRule between the remedies:\n13\t\n14\t(a) A guest execution/step budget at the test-harness or engine-safepoint level (the engineer flagged this as architect territory — it may touch the safepoint contract in yang.php.md / yin.vm semantics). If you rule this way, define the smallest contract change: where the budget lives (run-vm test harness vs the engine's safepoint marks), what happens on exhaustion (interrupt? the existing Interrupt exception?), and whether production (non-test) semantics change at all.\n15\t\n16\t(b) Re-tiering: move phpt-derived stress cases (gc_013 and friends) behind the ^:slow tag (or DATOM_SLOW_TESTS) so the quick tier stays bounded, accepting the slow tier grows.\n17\t\n18\tOr both (a) for production robustness, (b) immediately for lane stability.\n19\t\n20\tAlso rule whether the 93-minute shiva e2e sighting is closed as \"finite stress cost, not a defect\" or must stay open until the remedy lands. Cite the safepoint docs you rely on. Read-only: do not edit."}
