c.cursor-cell-numbering.md:780:recomputation budget stops 397 of the carriers at `[:label-bytes]`: a\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.cursor-cell-numbering.md:798:stop at 6a's retained recompute budget, 0 other decode failures.\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.cursor-cell-numbering.md:829:of it: no component runs, no trials, no `:search` budget. What the\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.cursor-cell-numbering.md:884:budget, D6; the review found the byte accounting unimplemented, the D6\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.cursor-cell-numbering.md:892:early budget abort restored, the probe's decoder in the production\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.derivations.md:653:(`import_test`, `linked_prelude_test`, `safepoint_test`), whose pinned\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.derivations.md:985:   (`py`), the `pysp` spec `(:ast (safepoint/module-spec (h/registry) a))`\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.derivations.md:989:   The test requires `yang.python.antlr.prelude`, `.safepoint`, `.lower`,\ndocs/design/yin.vm.ucf-revisions.md:4:history and the static safepoint-kind ruling in section 8.\ndocs/design/yin.vm.ucf-revisions.md:227:  bundles the UCF 7.9 outcome; `safepoints` derives the static half\ndocs/design/yin.vm.ucf-revisions.md:228:  of UCF 7.4.2, plus `:yin.safepoint/reasons` (ucf.cljc:351),\ndocs/design/yin.vm.ucf-revisions.md:312:correction is executable: `ucf.cljc`'s static safepoint map now\ndocs/design/yin.vm.ucf-revisions.md:313:publishes `:yin.safepoint/kinds` (`ucf/parking-kinds`) with the\ndocs/design/yin.vm.ucf-revisions.md:314:ruling's values, and `:yin.safepoint/reasons` is gone; `ucf_test`'s\ndocs/design/yin.vm.ucf-revisions.md:467:     through `:yin.safepoint/kinds`: the kinds gate pc eligibility\ndocs/design/yin.vm.ucf-revisions.md:542:`:yin.safepoint/segment`, `/engine`, `/pc`, `/stack-effect`,\ndocs/design/yin.vm.ucf-revisions.md:544:`safepoints` publishes `:yin.safepoint/reasons` (ucf.cljc:351)\ndocs/design/yin.vm.ucf-revisions.md:573:`:yin.safepoint/reasons` field. The Phase 1 field exceeds that map.\ndocs/design/yin.vm.ucf-revisions.md:583:M4 shall replace `:yin.safepoint/reasons` with\ndocs/design/yin.vm.ucf-revisions.md:584:`:yin.safepoint/kinds`, whose values are static possibilities from\ndocs/design/yin.vm.ucf-revisions.md:596:a naming correction to the Phase 1 safepoint API, not a new `v2`\ndocs/design/yin.vm.ucf-revisions.md:597:execution revision: `:yin.safepoint/reasons` was not a component named\ndocs/design/yin.vm.ucf-revisions.md:602:The lift driver must check the pc against the static safepoint set,\ndocs/design/yin.vm.ucf-revisions.md:622:UCF 7.11's safepoint harness must run each 7.4.1 row, including both\ndocs/design/yin.vm.ucf-revisions.md:655:Second, the `\"v3\"` canonicalizer and the stack-shaped safepoint halves\ndocs/design/yin.vm.ucf-revisions.md:659:safepoint facts and frame validator live in `yin.vm.semantic.code`,\ndocs/design/yin.vm.ucf-revisions.md:832:**I-9 — 2026-10-16, any-PC.** The current lift rejects active control and queued completed outcomes, while the holder runs unrestricted computation. Slices 6d-a, 6d-b and 6e extend the carrier to run states and complete scheduler products. 6d-a includes completed stream/FFI/link/install outcomes, cursor-update encoding, bounded bridge-aware fuel and closed-gate execution guards. 6d-b adds explicit state retention on tenure failure and holder migration from fuel boundaries. 6e extends backend layouts and transfer laws. Earlier static-safepoint-only lift prescriptions are historical. No compatibility promise is added.\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md:12:`test/yin/vm/ucf/safepoint_harness_test.cljc`). Revision 2 (2026-10-11)\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md:97:the safepoint harness · §6 code and task context in the carrier · §7\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md:142:9. **Preemptive migration at any pc is a primary invariant of `yin.vm`** (owner, 2026-10-17: \"preemptive migration, the ability to pause and continue at any PC, is a primary invariant of yin.vm. It is why yin.vm is defined as a continuation VM based on the CESK model. The UCF being only defined at a wait or parked state is a violation of this invariant\"). The carrier expresses the evaluator's complete task state between **any** two instructions, including the scheduler's products (remaining waits, completed wakes), not only its two delivery states; a safepoint is a boundary at which the program stops by itself. Slices 6d-a (carrier, reference lane), 6d-b (holder, custody, expiry) and 6e (backends) land it.\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md:640:frame from its state at a safepoint; `lift(lower(frame)) = frame` on\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md:1103:`:yin.k/not-at-safepoint` (UCF §7.4.2, as amended; the name is\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md:1110:`:yin.k/not-at-safepoint` rather than borrow its successor's pc.\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md:1202:## 5. The safepoint harness\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md:1208:module contexts and every refusal: lift at the safepoint, lower into a\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md:1210:uninterrupted reference run; `lift(lower(frame)) = frame`; the frame's\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md:1218:(`safepoint_harness_test.cljc:92-106`), whose expected results follow\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md:1230:the harness pins `1` for that one case (`safepoint_harness_test.cljc`,\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md:1268:of the old harness (`safepoint_harness_test.cljc:92-106`: `:bare`,\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md:1313:defined and otherwise refuses it `:export-missing`. **Amended 2026-10-16 (any-pc, owner invariant 2026-10-17).** A budgeted sweep can retain a child with active control at phase `:running`. Row 11 now obtains that state by real execution. The lower requires a `:running` child at phase `:running` and a `:blocked` child at phase `:parked`. Row 12 is row 10's child under tail delive