/yang.php.md-1243-+----+------------------------------------+------------------------------------+\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-1244-\n--\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-1395-Z-combinator per function and per loop, type hints parsed and dropped, `-10;`\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-1396-folded into a literal, and PHP `null` lowered to host `nil`. Its tokenizer has\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-1397-no modes (no HTML, no heredoc, no `<?=`). Replacing only its parser would keep\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-1398-every semantic defect. **Ruling: replace.** Nothing of the legacy lowering is\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-1399-reused; the Z-combinator encoding is superseded by self-applied `:loop`-marked\ndocs/design/yang.php.md:1400:lambdas with cells, which also makes safepoints and tail marks work.\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-1401-\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-1402-Migration mechanics (the F2 pattern):\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-1403-\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-1404-- The ANTLR frontend is installed in `yin.repl.frontends/standard` as a\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-1405-  new revision of `:yang/php` (the compiler frontend keeps its revision\n--\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-1916-   throw `Error` with PHP's fatal text. The warning text retains the written\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-1917-   kind. A refused path is not added to the included-files dict, so a later\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-1918-   `_once` retries delivery. Each record carries the structured refusal under\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-1919-   `:yang.php/refusal`.\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-1920-\ndocs/design/yang.php.md:1921:## 12. Safepoints\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-1922-\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-1923-- `:loop` and `:call` hooks (`phpsp`) serve signals: `pcntl_signal` handlers\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-1924-  run at hooks via `stream/poll!` on a signal stream, and\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-1925-  `pcntl_async_signals` is the default and only mode. A recursion-depth bound\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-1926-  is available if a composition wants one (PHP has none; default off