t, `ob_*`); inclusion (`_once`, return\ndocs/design/yang.php.md:1970:  values, scope sharing, the two missing-include stages); safepoints (tick\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-1971-  counts, a signal at a hook).\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-1972-- **Fixture groups** are those of section 4.6, plus a request-record fixture\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-1973-  per corpus program. Corners are departure fixtures whose expected value is\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-1974-  the recorded deviation.\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-1975-\n--\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-2090-|       |                                  | `require_once` throw `Error`; a   |\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-2091-|       |                                  | refused `_once` retries delivery  |\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-2092-+-------+----------------------------------+-----------------------------------+\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-2093-| P7-a  | signals: `phpsp` hooks at        | a signal at a `:loop` hook runs   |\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-2094-|       | `:loop` and `:call`,             | the handler; an empty signal      |\ndocs/design/yang.php.md:2095:|       | `pcntl_signal`, the safepoint    | stream never parks; budget        |\ndocs/design/yang.php.md:2096:|       | budget                           | exhaustion raises the pinned      |\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-2097-|       |                                  | fatal text                        |\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-2098-+-------+----------------------------------+-----------------------------------+\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-2099-| P7-b  | ticks: `declare(ticks)`,         | tick counts equal PHP's for the   |\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-2100-|       | `register_tick_function`; behind | statement fixture                 |\ndocs/design/yang.php.md:2101:|       | safepoint slice 3                |                                   |\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-2102-+-------+----------------------------------+-----------------------------------+\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-2103-| P8    | legacy retirement: the legacy    | the REPL prints `1` for `<?php $x |\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-2104-|       | test programs in the new corpus, | = 1; echo $x;`; every legacy test |\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-2105-|       | the demo on checked-in CST       | program passes with corrected     |\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-2106-|       | packets,                         | expectations; the demo runs its   |\n--\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-2315-|                     | in P4                               |                  |\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-2316-+---------------------+-------------------------------------+------------------+\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-2317-| C21 memory and time | Engine: `memory_limit`,             | restricted; none |\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-2318-| limits              | `max_execution_time`,               | (operational)    |\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-2319-|                     | `memory_get_usage`. Here: the       |                  |\ndocs/design/yang.php.md:2320:|                     | deterministic safepoint budget and  |                  |\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-2321-|                     | no memory accounting;               |                  |\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-2322-|                     | `memory_get_usage` returns a pinned |                  |\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-2323-|                     | constant                            |                  |\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-2324-+---------------------+-------------------------------------+------------------+\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-2325-| C22 destructor      | Engine: destructor `echo` inside an | specified,       |\n--\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-2472-3. (B8.3) The dynamic-scope profile rule (recommended) versus dict scopes for\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-2473-   every function (simpler, slower, and it loses the cell path).\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-2474-4. (B8.4) Warnings as diagnostic-stream records (recommended) versus a guest\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-2475-   `Warning` exception class; the 