{"role":"assistant","content":"## Ruling: both, sequenced\n\n**(b) Re-tier immediately.** Keep ordinary PHPT cases in the quick tier, but move the curated PHPT stress cases—at minimum `gc_013`, `gc_023`, and their e2e-derived counterparts—behind `^:slow` / `DATOM_SLOW_TESTS`. Do not reduce iteration counts or otherwise alter fixture semantics. The current combined quick test is at `test/yang/php/antlr/e2e_test.clj:340`.\n\n**(a) Add the budget as a separate P7-a robustness change, not as a prerequisite for lane stability.**\n\nSmallest contract:\n\n- Add an **optional, per-run safepoint-count budget** to the PHP execution profile. `run-vm` may pass the option, but must not implement a host wall-clock timeout as guest semantics.\n- Count the existing PHP `:loop` and `:call` safepoint hooks; do not introduce generic VM-instruction accounting for this feature.\n- Default is **unlimited/off**, so production behavior is unchanged unless a composition explicitly supplies a budget.\n- Exhaustion is the documented **PHP operational fatal**, using the pinned PHP text—not the JavaScript `Interrupt` exception. It is not guest-catchable and skips destructor shutdown, consistent with `docs/design/yang.php.md:1239` and `docs/design/yang.php.md:1927`.\n- This bounds guest execution between hooks; it is not a wall-clock guarantee around blocking host operations.\n\nThis follows the existing PHP contract: deterministic safepoint budget rather than nondeterministic `max_execution_time` (`docs/design/yang.php.md:1921-1938`, `docs/design/yang.php.md:2093-2097`). Generic engine step budgets remain an engine responsibility (`docs/design/yin.vm.engine.md:565-568`); safepoints are program stopping boundaries, not a license to change default execution semantics (`docs/design/yin.vm.semantic.md:655-659`).\n\n**Disposition of the 93-minute shiva sighting:** close the suspected **guest-nontermination defect now** as finite stress cost, supported by the fixture walk and measured `gc_013` completion (`collab/1793540000000-engineer-p4-hang.gpt-6-luna.findings.md:9-21`). Keep the **quick-tier lane-stability task** open until re-tiering lands; do not hold the hang investigation open for the budget work."}
